# Linear: no posting without approval

Never create or update Linear content on the user's behalf without **explicit approval of the exact content first**.

## Applies to

- Comments (`save_comment`) — including replies and thread posts
- Issues (`save_issue`) — title, description, status, assignee, or any field change
- Documents, project updates, diff reviews, and any other Linear MCP write action

## Required workflow

1. Draft the full message or change in the chat (markdown as it will appear in Linear).
2. Ask the user to approve, edit, or reject — e.g. "Reply on MR-529?" with the draft visible.
3. Call Linear MCP write tools **only** after the user explicitly approves (e.g. "post it", "yes", "go ahead").

## Do not post when

- The user only asked what to say, how to reply, or to "mention X in the thread"
- The user asked for a rundown, summary, or draft without saying to post
- Approval was for a different version of the text than what you are about to send

## Safe without approval

- Read-only Linear MCP (`list_issues`, `get_issue`, `list_comments`, etc.)
- Showing a draft in chat for review

## Examples

```
# ❌ BAD — user said "I'd like to mention this in the thread"
→ immediately calls save_comment

# ✅ GOOD
→ draft reply in chat, ask "Post this on MR-529?"
→ user says "post it"
→ save_comment with approved text
```
